WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.007
[theme music playing]

01:03.313 --> 01:05.982
GENIE, MAKE A WISH

01:17.535 --> 01:18.828
[phone vibrates]

01:24.292 --> 01:26.461
PLEASE RETURN YOUR ID
AND YOUR LOCKER AND BUILDING KEYS

01:26.544 --> 01:29.297
Gu Bo-gyeong, I'm holding you
responsible for this. You're fired!

01:29.380 --> 01:31.800
What will you do
about our branch's average balance?

01:34.761 --> 01:39.474
Fuck! [sighs]

01:39.557 --> 01:40.391
[Da-jin] A genie?

01:40.975 --> 01:42.060
That's nonsense.

01:42.143 --> 01:44.604
Our channel went viral
because you found that corpse.

01:44.687 --> 01:48.274
Yeah, and the genie is the one
who helped me find the corpse.

01:48.358 --> 01:49.484
I'm being serious!

01:49.567 --> 01:53.113
Otherwise, how could I possibly
have found that corpse?

01:53.613 --> 01:55.698
You have to believe me.

01:56.741 --> 01:59.577
We only have two chances left, Da-jin.

01:59.661 --> 02:00.745
We're both SKY grads.

02:00.829 --> 02:05.458
We need to rack our brains and figure out
how to turn our lives around, okay?

02:10.797 --> 02:11.840
[groans]

02:13.675 --> 02:17.303
If it's a wish, could we wish
to inherit a conglomerate fortune?

02:17.387 --> 02:21.349
[sighs] Why inherit it? We could
just become the conglomerates.

02:22.308 --> 02:25.520
Hold up. How much
is the richest person in Korea worth?

02:25.603 --> 02:28.523
Do we really need that much?
It's not like we're building an empire.

02:28.606 --> 02:30.108
Say we have two kids.

02:30.191 --> 02:33.069
If we fund their studies abroad
and a home for when they marry,

02:33.153 --> 02:35.280
that's billions already.
What about retirement?

02:35.363 --> 02:37.782
You're right. You can never have too much.

02:38.408 --> 02:40.285
But are you sure there are no conditions?

02:41.202 --> 02:43.121
In any fables with spirits,

02:43.204 --> 02:45.915
the moral is always
"what goes around comes around."

02:45.999 --> 02:49.919
"Pigs get fat, hogs get slaughtered."
What if there's a price?

02:50.712 --> 02:52.172
[sighs]

02:52.255 --> 02:54.299
-It would be nice if we could ask.
-Hey!

02:54.883 --> 02:57.176
What if the genie answers
and counts it as a wish?

02:57.260 --> 03:01.264
[gasps] You're right.
[sighs, clicks tongue]

03:02.599 --> 03:04.851
Then how about
we think about it separately

03:04.934 --> 03:06.978
and each get to use one wish?

03:07.061 --> 03:08.021
What?

03:08.813 --> 03:11.649
-But… why would I do that?
-Uh--

03:11.733 --> 03:14.611
[scoffs] I wouldn't have told you
if we were going to do that.

03:15.320 --> 03:18.031
Uh, we're a married couple,
so isn't it a given?

03:18.531 --> 03:20.825
We can make money,
but some things money can't buy.

03:22.076 --> 03:23.536
What are you thinking about?

03:24.871 --> 03:26.623
Wishing for Dad to be cancer-free.

03:26.706 --> 03:30.043
[groans] Come on, we have modern medicine.

03:30.126 --> 03:33.296
Why would you wish
for something like that?

03:33.379 --> 03:34.797
Money would solve everything.

03:35.506 --> 03:37.383
My dad has terminal liver cancer.

03:37.884 --> 03:39.344
Terminal means there's no hope.

03:39.427 --> 03:42.222
Come on, it's not like
he's on his deathbed or anything.

03:42.805 --> 03:43.890
Check out our views.

03:43.973 --> 03:47.727
We'll be generating income in no time,
so let's just wait three months.

03:47.810 --> 03:49.812
We'll just save the wish for now, okay?

03:49.896 --> 03:51.105
Hey, Ko Yeong-hyeon.

03:51.814 --> 03:53.358
Fuck you!

03:54.108 --> 03:56.653
[clacking, thudding]

04:10.250 --> 04:12.377
[soft tense music playing]

04:18.341 --> 04:20.510
[breathing deeply]

04:20.593 --> 04:23.137
-[yells in frustration]
-[clatters]

04:23.221 --> 04:26.766
[breath trembling]

04:26.849 --> 04:27.684
[Shadi] Khalid!

04:28.351 --> 04:29.394
Khalid!

04:30.895 --> 04:34.941
[in Arabic] I saw Iblis!
I saw him bringing humans to ruin.

04:35.525 --> 04:38.528
It was truly a sight to behold, Father.

04:38.611 --> 04:40.446
Tell me what you did.

04:40.530 --> 04:41.572
Did you hurt the girl?

04:42.198 --> 04:46.286
I feel no pain in this body,
nor do I feel out of breath.

04:46.869 --> 04:49.664
But I do not have power like Iblis.

04:49.747 --> 04:51.416
I have lost my ability to weave,

04:51.499 --> 04:55.920
so what am I to do now
with this immortal body?

04:56.421 --> 04:59.424
-[tense music playing]
-[Shadi breathing heavily]

05:09.809 --> 05:12.520
[in Korean] The end is near!

05:13.021 --> 05:15.189
You foolish humans!

05:15.690 --> 05:19.277
Judgment day is approaching!

05:19.360 --> 05:23.281
Angels from the sky alert us!
Heed me when I say…

05:23.364 --> 05:26.326
[sighs] I'll let it slide today.
I have a lot on my mind.

05:27.452 --> 05:30.413
Then you shall all be saved.

05:34.792 --> 05:36.961
[tense music playing]

05:38.921 --> 05:39.881
[sighs]

05:44.927 --> 05:47.638
You said I stole a feather of yours
before I was locked up.

05:48.139 --> 05:51.267
Again with your damn feather talk.
I don't know about it.

05:51.350 --> 05:53.644
Well, I do. I know what I did with it.

05:54.562 --> 05:56.064
I wrote some things.

05:56.147 --> 05:58.733
On the floors and columns,
all over my lamp.

06:00.860 --> 06:03.780
You figured that out?

06:03.863 --> 06:06.365
Yes, but I'm not sure
when I could have done it.

06:07.158 --> 06:08.242
Nor do I remember.

06:10.078 --> 06:12.371
[Ka-young] So please

06:12.872 --> 06:14.624
make sure we are punished.

06:14.707 --> 06:16.709
You and I both.

06:17.210 --> 06:19.295
That final wish Ki Ka-young made

06:20.129 --> 06:21.506
was fulfilled.

06:22.006 --> 06:23.007
Right?

06:23.966 --> 06:27.011
He brought Ki Ka-young back to life
to carry out that final wish,

06:27.095 --> 06:30.848
and I was reunited
with the reincarnated Ki Ka-young.

06:31.349 --> 06:32.433
Am I wrong?

06:33.684 --> 06:35.686
If my fury was enough to level a city…

06:36.187 --> 06:42.151
HABIBTI

06:42.235 --> 06:43.986
…it must mean I had lost a loved one.

06:44.487 --> 06:45.613
I'd lost Ki Ka-young.

06:47.907 --> 06:49.450
I must have loved her.

06:50.034 --> 06:51.911
-Isn't that right?
-So what?

06:52.703 --> 06:54.539
Are we playing bingo? What's your point?

06:54.622 --> 06:55.998
About Ki Ka-young's lifespan.

06:57.250 --> 06:58.167
You must be mad.

06:58.251 --> 06:59.585
How much is left?

06:59.669 --> 07:00.837
I beg you.

07:02.463 --> 07:03.714
Tell me so I can prepare.

07:03.798 --> 07:05.091
All because of a lowly human!

07:06.801 --> 07:08.886
Have you learned nothing
from Shadi's fate?

07:08.970 --> 07:10.096
Of course not.

07:11.973 --> 07:15.351
Why else would I be doing everything I can
not to kill the immortal one?

07:16.602 --> 07:19.105
Shadi loves that boy enough
to die for him,

07:20.523 --> 07:21.732
and because he loves him,

07:23.401 --> 07:24.819
the pain cuts deep.

07:28.239 --> 07:29.991
You arrogant shaytan.

07:30.575 --> 07:33.995
If you're so curious, pluck out my eyes
to see for yourself. Go ahead.

07:34.495 --> 07:37.665
I wonder why he keeps
forgiving a bastard like you.

07:47.258 --> 07:50.136
Who shall stand in the day of judgment?

07:50.219 --> 07:53.306
Who will walk the path to salvation?

07:57.477 --> 07:59.854
[breath trembling]

08:00.771 --> 08:03.774
[crows cawing]

08:03.858 --> 08:04.692
[Irem sighs]

08:06.611 --> 08:09.739
[door opens and closes]

08:14.243 --> 08:16.871
I was gathering intel on the immortal one.

08:17.371 --> 08:20.583
I sensed that your intentions
were aligned with the immortal one.

08:21.542 --> 08:24.754
The half-spirit is clawing his way up,
not knowing his place,

08:24.837 --> 08:28.466
while Iblis and Ki Ka-young are edging
closer to the truth of their past lives.

08:29.425 --> 08:32.303
And now, even my mythical beast
is totally missing the mark?

08:32.803 --> 08:34.096
What now, Irem?

08:34.597 --> 08:37.850
If you could just…
point me in the right direction--

08:37.934 --> 08:39.560
What do you think I'm doing now?

08:42.104 --> 08:42.939
Listen carefully.

08:43.731 --> 08:45.650
No, wait. You can't hear, can you?

08:46.651 --> 08:47.485
[chuckles]

08:48.152 --> 08:49.237
Watch carefully.

08:51.239 --> 08:55.618
The half-spirit will use Shadi
and plunge the world into sleep once more.

08:56.661 --> 08:58.996
When that day comes,
there is something you must do.

08:59.497 --> 09:01.207
That's all you need to do.

09:02.542 --> 09:03.668
Am I understood?

09:06.546 --> 09:09.090
Yes, Master.

09:11.133 --> 09:12.718
[beeping]

09:14.262 --> 09:15.596
-[chimes]
-[Heung-rye] Hmm?

09:16.597 --> 09:17.682
These brats.

09:19.308 --> 09:20.685
ELDEST

09:22.395 --> 09:26.857
Hey, I've brought over some side dishes,
but your door won't seem to open.

09:26.941 --> 09:29.402
I must be entering the wrong code.

09:29.485 --> 09:33.030
[son] I told you not to come.
You know my wife's gone on a cruise.

09:33.114 --> 09:35.908
That's why I cooked you food.
I'll just pop it inside--

09:35.992 --> 09:37.493
[son] Just leave it at the door.

09:37.577 --> 09:40.121
My wife doesn't want anyone
who's not family in the house.

09:40.204 --> 09:42.415
You rotten bastard!
Aren't I family to you?

09:42.498 --> 09:44.709
Am I a stranger? Am I?

09:44.792 --> 09:46.210
You little…

09:46.294 --> 09:48.629
[indistinct chatter]

09:48.713 --> 09:52.967
-Stop eating and get peeling.
-[all laughing]

09:53.718 --> 09:56.554
You're back early
from visiting your son, the judge.

09:56.637 --> 09:57.888
Yes.

09:57.972 --> 10:01.559
He kept asking me to stay over,
saying he'd send me on a cruise,

10:01.642 --> 10:04.145
but I couldn't be bothered,
so I just came back.

10:04.687 --> 10:07.273
How lucky you are. [chuckles]

10:07.356 --> 10:09.108
[cell phones chime]

10:09.191 --> 10:11.611
Mm? What is this?

10:13.863 --> 10:14.697
OH PAN-GEUM

10:14.780 --> 10:18.200
[Pan-geum] I think I'll be going
farther away than Hawaii.

10:18.284 --> 10:20.328
Please take good care of my Ka-young.

10:20.411 --> 10:21.579
Where's she off to now?

10:21.662 --> 10:24.332
Her daughter must be
treating her incredibly well.

10:24.832 --> 10:27.293
If it's farther away than Hawaii,
how nice must it be?

10:27.376 --> 10:31.130
What's so great about being flown around
at a ripe old age? What a bother!

10:31.213 --> 10:34.967
Hawaii? That old place?
I could go tomorrow if I wanted to.

10:35.468 --> 10:40.222
My eldest son is a judge, and my youngest
is an executive at a major conglomerate.

10:40.306 --> 10:42.808
And my grandchildren are all geniuses.

10:42.892 --> 10:44.060
Just look at Ok-nam.

10:44.644 --> 10:48.481
She abandoned her entire life
and ran away because of her child.

10:49.106 --> 10:52.276
If anyone thinks they did a better job
at raising their kids than me,

10:52.360 --> 10:53.235
come on out, I say!

10:53.319 --> 10:56.572
Of course. Right you are!

10:56.656 --> 11:01.035
-We all know. We all do.
-[everyone chuckles]

11:01.118 --> 11:02.453
AN BOK-JA

11:03.996 --> 11:08.918
[Bok-ja] Don't worry about Ka-young,
and send us some photos of the nice place.

11:09.001 --> 11:12.463
[sighs] I wonder
where Ok-nam has gotten to.

11:13.464 --> 11:16.008
She even changed her number.

11:19.303 --> 11:22.431
-What is that smell? Is it chicken soup?
-Yes.

11:23.057 --> 11:25.309
Tell that tall fellow to come too.

11:26.560 --> 11:27.686
[grunts softly]

11:28.479 --> 11:32.566
I hope you'll continue to get along
with my dear Ka-young.

11:33.067 --> 11:35.736
Don't fight, and you mustn't leave her.

11:35.820 --> 11:38.906
If she acts all prickly,
just be gentle with her.

11:38.989 --> 11:40.282
[Iblis] Mm-mm.

11:43.828 --> 11:46.956
-The drumsticks are always mine.
-Goodness me.

11:47.665 --> 11:50.292
Just play nice and share. Hmm.

11:50.793 --> 11:52.503
What's yours is his, even a bean.

11:52.586 --> 11:56.882
For better or worse,
until death do you part.

11:56.966 --> 11:59.176
Then give him beans.
The drumsticks are mine.

11:59.260 --> 12:00.428
You brat!

12:00.511 --> 12:03.472
Just let him have one today!
I'm doing all of this for a reason.

12:03.556 --> 12:05.891
What reason?
The drumsticks are mine, so why?

12:06.600 --> 12:09.061
-Don't you dare touch my…
-[rooster crowing in background]

12:09.979 --> 12:13.315
-[cutlery clatters]
-Come here.

12:17.445 --> 12:19.363
-You come here.
-[Mi-ju sighs]

12:19.447 --> 12:21.031
-I said to come here.
-I said no.

12:21.115 --> 12:22.324
[Mi-ju sighs]

12:23.117 --> 12:24.034
Do you want to die?

12:24.118 --> 12:25.161
[dramatic music playing]

12:25.786 --> 12:27.746
-I'd rather not.
-Don't talk back!

12:27.830 --> 12:29.123
Don't ask questions!

12:29.790 --> 12:32.209
-I said not to talk back.
-I said not to ask questions!

12:32.293 --> 12:33.377
[Ka-young] Stop copying me!

12:33.461 --> 12:36.672
This level of chemistry
is good enough for me.

12:36.755 --> 12:38.757
-[Ka-young] Get over here!
-[Iblis laughs]

12:38.841 --> 12:40.593
[Ka-young screaming and grunting]

12:52.855 --> 12:55.774
Mm. Seeing as this word comes up the most,

12:55.858 --> 12:58.319
is this habibti? "My love"?

12:58.402 --> 13:01.155
What? Right, yes. It is.

13:01.780 --> 13:04.116
-You don't even remember, but this is me?
-Mm?

13:04.200 --> 13:07.495
There's a 50-50 chance it's me or Jinniya.

13:09.121 --> 13:12.458
Shouldn't you have cleared up
those doubts before we kissed?

13:14.418 --> 13:16.170
If this happens to be Jinniya,

13:17.254 --> 13:19.882
you will die for exploiting my hard labor.

13:21.050 --> 13:22.510
So hurry and find your memories.

13:23.677 --> 13:25.054
[Iblis] I've found one.

13:25.679 --> 13:30.684
It says, "Every night you make a garment
to wear when you return to Goryeo."

13:32.520 --> 13:33.354
A garment?

13:33.437 --> 13:37.233
Hmm. I guess I must have liked
needles back then too.

13:37.775 --> 13:39.360
-[Iblis] Hmm?
-[wrench clatters]

13:39.944 --> 13:41.195
Where is Khalid's name?

13:41.987 --> 13:43.906
Here and here.

13:44.865 --> 13:45.741
Why?

13:45.824 --> 13:49.036
Because, in Korea,
it's unlucky to write names in red.

13:50.037 --> 13:50.871
This brat.

13:51.539 --> 13:56.043
If this is when he started preparing,
then we're losing on all fronts.

13:59.129 --> 14:00.965
We're completely winning at one thing.

14:01.674 --> 14:05.261
No matter how much information Khalid has,
you'll be the one making the wish.

14:07.763 --> 14:08.931
Let's get out of here.

14:09.431 --> 14:11.767
From now on,
you and the lamp are inseparable.

14:13.894 --> 14:15.646
You want me to carry it around?

14:16.939 --> 14:18.148
Like a portable

14:18.816 --> 14:19.650
curry pot.

14:20.442 --> 14:21.569
That's believable, right?

14:22.361 --> 14:23.362
That's why…

14:25.489 --> 14:26.323
Here.

14:27.741 --> 14:30.160
I saw people carrying these things around.

14:31.287 --> 14:33.747
-Not bad at adapting.
-Mm-hmm.

14:36.959 --> 14:39.461
I wonder how much time we have left.

14:44.091 --> 14:46.719
On that note,
listen carefully to what I say now.

14:47.678 --> 14:51.181
I'm sure Khalid will use Shadi again
to try to tie me up.

14:52.016 --> 14:55.561
If that moment comes, and I am tied up,

14:57.229 --> 14:59.940
you must use your final wish
to save yourself.

15:00.983 --> 15:04.028
You must make a righteous wish. Got it?

15:07.072 --> 15:09.575
It seems you've decided where you'll go.

15:13.662 --> 15:16.123
-Well, I'll never let you go.
-[chuckles]

15:18.000 --> 15:20.127
I knew that wouldn't work. [chuckles]

15:28.093 --> 15:31.972
[Yeong-hyeon] By the way,
do psychopaths really not feel love?

15:32.556 --> 15:35.559
You know, being ready
to give your life for someone else.

15:35.643 --> 15:37.061
I would be willing

15:37.937 --> 15:39.396
to kill for someone else.

15:40.272 --> 15:42.483
-Doesn't that count as love?
-[key clacks]

15:43.567 --> 15:44.985
Hey, Choi Da-jin. Look at this!

15:45.069 --> 15:48.113
That old interview we did
with the psychopath is blowing up again!

15:48.197 --> 15:50.407
It's trending at number nine! [laughs]

15:51.325 --> 15:53.160
There's even a meme in the comments…

15:54.328 --> 15:58.207
"I worked late instead of my manager.
Doesn't that count as love?"

15:58.290 --> 16:01.627
"I binged on food instead of my boyfriend.
Doesn't that count as love?"

16:01.710 --> 16:04.421
"I only ate the tails
of the fish-shaped pastry for you."

16:04.505 --> 16:07.716
Only the tails? That's mental. [laughs]

16:07.800 --> 16:09.593
This is fucking hilarious.

16:10.094 --> 16:11.178
So what will we do

16:12.554 --> 16:14.056
about the wishes?

16:15.516 --> 16:18.602
You're talking about that again?
[sighs wearily]

16:18.686 --> 16:20.020
I'm so sick of this.

16:20.521 --> 16:24.024
Let's just enjoy the moment
for a while! [sighs]

16:24.108 --> 16:25.401
[sighs]

16:26.568 --> 16:27.486
No.

16:30.239 --> 16:31.740
Let's just get a divorce.

16:32.324 --> 16:33.158
What?

16:33.242 --> 16:37.162
You said you had two wishes left, right?
Give me one of them as alimony.

16:37.246 --> 16:38.497
A divorce?

16:39.373 --> 16:41.542
[sighs] Have you gone insane?

16:42.167 --> 16:43.210
Hey.

16:43.293 --> 16:46.588
Frankly speaking, they're my wishes.
Who do you think you are?

16:47.256 --> 16:50.342
Right. This is how
you really feel, isn't it?

16:51.468 --> 16:52.344
Son of a bitch.

16:53.512 --> 16:56.682
What? Hey, what did you
just call me? Son of a bitch?

16:57.850 --> 17:01.103
This person really is Oh Pan-geum?

17:01.186 --> 17:02.980
That's right, Oh Pan-geum.

17:03.063 --> 17:05.232
The third daughter
of the lady from Bukcheon.

17:05.315 --> 17:09.236
She was the prettiest thing in Hadong
and moved to Seoul when she got married.

17:09.319 --> 17:11.196
That smile is her, all right.

17:11.780 --> 17:14.116
Her husband was from Chungcheong-do.

17:14.199 --> 17:17.494
Last I heard,
both their daughters got married.

17:18.120 --> 17:19.121
Let me take a look.

17:20.831 --> 17:24.168
My word! This was when
she was a young thing.

17:24.251 --> 17:26.378
But why are you looking for her anyway?

17:26.462 --> 17:28.464
What is it? Did Pan-geum here die?

17:30.340 --> 17:32.634
No, she's very healthy.

17:32.718 --> 17:34.636
[woman sighs in relief]
That's good to hear.

17:35.721 --> 17:36.805
[Min-ji exhales]

17:39.266 --> 17:40.309
[exhales]

17:40.392 --> 17:42.644
[Ka-young] I'm not quite sure
what he does for a living.

17:42.728 --> 17:44.730
He mostly tells me to make a wish.

17:44.813 --> 17:47.107
Holy smokes, my teeth must have
gotten younger too.

17:47.191 --> 17:49.860
Don't ask me anything about those two.

17:49.943 --> 17:50.903
My deal?

17:50.986 --> 17:53.822
[Ka-young] One thing I know for certain
is that he isn't human.

17:54.406 --> 17:56.408
If I can't ask anything…

17:58.327 --> 17:59.578
and he isn't human

18:00.287 --> 18:02.289
and asks people to make wishes…

18:04.416 --> 18:08.504
[laughing]

18:08.587 --> 18:09.630
[exclaims]

18:09.713 --> 18:11.965
I'm so stunned, all I can do is laugh.

18:14.760 --> 18:16.720
Why? Just wear them out.

18:16.804 --> 18:18.764
I just want to buy you something.

18:19.348 --> 18:22.351
Wear these and go wherever you want to go.

18:22.935 --> 18:24.603
Wherever that may be,

18:25.646 --> 18:27.397
I'm sure it'll be the right path.

18:28.482 --> 18:29.316
Okay?

18:33.487 --> 18:36.365
[sniffles]

18:36.448 --> 18:38.033
If Mi-ju…

18:40.244 --> 18:42.121
[sniffles] …is actually Grandma…

18:43.789 --> 18:46.166
[sobbing]

18:57.052 --> 18:58.804
[liquid dripping]

19:28.083 --> 19:31.670
[Pan-geum] Ka-young.
This is the soybean paste jar.

19:32.421 --> 19:34.673
Once every month, open the lid

19:34.756 --> 19:38.886
to check for mold growing on the surface
beneath the top salt layer

19:38.969 --> 19:41.763
and for signs of bugs.

19:42.639 --> 19:43.807
[sighs]

19:45.184 --> 19:46.894
[inhales, sighs]

19:46.977 --> 19:50.189
[Pan-geum] When the weather is nice,
leave the lid open so it gets some sun.

19:50.689 --> 19:52.357
This is the soy sauce jar.

19:52.441 --> 19:53.567
[crying]

19:53.650 --> 19:56.403
If you happen to see
any white patches of mold,

19:56.486 --> 20:00.699
scoop them away,
give it a good boil, and pour it back in.

20:01.992 --> 20:02.826
[sniffles]

20:03.911 --> 20:06.288
[crying]

20:16.256 --> 20:19.009
-[bowl clangs]
-[sighs]

20:25.557 --> 20:27.351
That means I'll be fine

20:28.435 --> 20:29.561
until next spring.

20:30.479 --> 20:31.855
That's good enough.

20:33.232 --> 20:36.944
People die of accidents or illness.

20:38.237 --> 20:40.906
It wouldn't be all that strange
to die at this age anyway.

20:44.159 --> 20:46.536
Oh, my. You're up already?

20:47.120 --> 20:48.872
You should sleep in on your day off.

20:48.956 --> 20:50.874
I need to go to the workshop.

20:52.459 --> 20:55.003
But, Grandma, why do you keep
looking at that tree?

21:19.611 --> 21:20.654
What are you doing?

21:21.238 --> 21:23.031
Thinking about whether to fix it.

21:23.115 --> 21:24.950
But from here,

21:25.742 --> 21:28.954
I have the point of view
of a corpse buried in a hole.

21:29.538 --> 21:31.498
You sure have a way with words.

21:32.499 --> 21:34.418
[wind blowing]

21:37.421 --> 21:39.298
Would this mean we're buried together?

21:39.881 --> 21:41.883
You're going to make things
this easy for me?

21:48.598 --> 21:51.018
Should we go for a carpet ride tomorrow?

21:51.768 --> 21:52.602
You can.

21:54.563 --> 21:56.982
I'm going to Seoul with Grandma tomorrow.

21:57.482 --> 21:59.151
You ride your carpet

21:59.651 --> 22:01.236
and fix the roof.

22:02.237 --> 22:03.238
Why Seoul?

22:04.906 --> 22:08.327
Because I want Grandma to have
some ordinary memories of me.

22:12.789 --> 22:13.999
All right.

22:19.671 --> 22:21.631
I have one of those to make too.

22:22.799 --> 22:25.802
[gentle music playing]

22:26.636 --> 22:28.930
-[rapid clicking]
-[Sang-hyeok exclaiming]

22:29.431 --> 22:30.724
[character groans]

22:30.807 --> 22:33.685
-[whimpering]
-Sweet! A KO win!

22:33.769 --> 22:34.770
You little…

22:37.189 --> 22:38.774
I need to go home now.

22:38.857 --> 22:41.777
Hey, that's not fair.
I haven't won a single game yet.

22:41.860 --> 22:45.113
You should go home soon too, mister.
There's no place like home.

22:46.615 --> 22:48.950
That sure doesn't sound like you.

22:49.743 --> 22:52.746
-Did you buy a house, by any chance?
-That's not funny.

22:53.371 --> 22:55.957
You can't tell anyone this,

22:56.666 --> 22:59.419
-but an angel granted my wish.
-[chuckles]

22:59.920 --> 23:02.506
Mom's boyfriend disappeared.

23:03.507 --> 23:07.385
It's time I cut back on arcade games
so my mom doesn't worry.

23:10.514 --> 23:12.390
I didn't expect this kind of fallout.

23:14.684 --> 23:15.769
Kim Sang-hyeok!

23:18.105 --> 23:19.106
It's been really fun.

23:20.232 --> 23:22.025
And you're my bro.

23:24.611 --> 23:25.529
Never forget that.

23:26.363 --> 23:27.405
What's with you?

23:27.489 --> 23:30.826
I said I'd cut back.
I didn't say I'd quit entirely.

23:31.409 --> 23:32.702
See you tomorrow.

23:45.841 --> 23:46.925
[chuckles softly]

23:49.344 --> 23:50.595
-[thuds]
-[Mi-ju sighs]

23:50.679 --> 23:52.430
[sighs] You're not going?

23:53.014 --> 23:53.849
Why not?

23:53.932 --> 23:57.310
It's the department store.
The new winter collection's out.

23:58.103 --> 23:59.521
-I have a lot of clothes.
-[thuds]

24:00.188 --> 24:02.399
I have plenty to last me
until next February.

24:03.692 --> 24:04.860
Instead…

24:06.653 --> 24:07.988
let's go somewhere else.

24:09.698 --> 24:10.699
Where exactly?

24:12.742 --> 24:14.578
You wanted to come here?

24:16.037 --> 24:17.205
Why?

24:17.706 --> 24:20.250
Because I want to be pretty
in your memories.

24:21.751 --> 24:25.255
Don't I look pretty? Don't I look cute?
Aren't I just to die for?

24:27.549 --> 24:28.884
In my memories?

24:30.969 --> 24:33.513
Why does it seem like
she has the same idea as me?

24:36.892 --> 24:38.768
-Smile.
-[camera shutter clicks]

24:38.852 --> 24:42.939
-[chuckling] Like this.
-[camera shutter clicking]

24:43.023 --> 24:44.733
-[whimpers]
-Hurry and do this!

24:44.816 --> 24:45.984
[camera shutter clicking]

24:46.067 --> 24:47.068
Like this? Maybe?

24:47.611 --> 24:49.905
-[camera shutter clicks]
-All right. [giggles]

24:49.988 --> 24:51.156
[camera shutter clicks]

24:51.239 --> 24:52.199
[Mi-ju chuckles]

24:53.700 --> 24:54.784
Oh, boy!

24:55.368 --> 24:56.745
How pretty.

24:58.705 --> 25:00.290
Why do people even do this?

25:00.373 --> 25:02.459
Why not? It's so much fun.

25:03.418 --> 25:06.171
Let's have coffee and enjoy ourselves
just a little longer.

25:06.254 --> 25:09.507
Go and buy me something sweet, all right?

25:10.008 --> 25:11.218
-Fine.
-Great.

25:12.510 --> 25:15.138
[chuckles] Goodness me.

25:15.639 --> 25:16.723
[chuckles]

25:20.101 --> 25:21.144
[chuckles]

25:27.484 --> 25:29.486
[chuckles and sniffles]

25:29.569 --> 25:30.403
[sighs]

26:09.818 --> 26:12.320
Half the lights on your sign are out.

26:12.821 --> 26:14.656
Trying to tell the world you're single?

26:16.074 --> 26:17.867
I saw that too.

26:19.119 --> 26:21.246
I smell gamja-tang.

26:22.247 --> 26:23.415
It must be Wednesday.

26:23.498 --> 26:26.209
I got it to go, though,
from a different place.

26:27.294 --> 26:28.128
Let's eat.

26:30.130 --> 26:32.299
I thought you'd get mad at me.

26:32.382 --> 26:34.217
This is your routine.

26:39.639 --> 26:43.226
CHEONGPUNG VILLAGE HALL

26:43.310 --> 26:45.145
[intriguing music plays]

26:48.023 --> 26:50.650
Oh. Grandma? How is Hawaii?

26:51.735 --> 26:53.069
Ka-young is well.

26:53.653 --> 26:55.822
Have you tried the coconut shrimp yet?

26:56.323 --> 26:58.033
That sounds delicious.

26:58.533 --> 27:00.035
Bullshit.

27:00.535 --> 27:03.705
She's not somewhere nicer.
She's still in Hawaii.

27:05.123 --> 27:06.666
[Min-ji laughs]

27:28.355 --> 27:29.189
[Mi-ju sighs]

27:34.611 --> 27:35.987
[Mi-ju sighs]

27:39.199 --> 27:42.702
I'm going to stop holding
the ancestral rites now.

27:44.037 --> 27:45.663
This is the last time.

27:47.791 --> 27:48.917
Why?

27:49.000 --> 27:51.252
We've already done enough.

27:52.545 --> 27:53.880
When I die,

27:54.381 --> 27:55.965
don't bother with any rites.

27:56.049 --> 27:57.759
Don't do a thing.

27:58.676 --> 28:01.262
Cremate me and scatter my ashes somewhere.

28:04.307 --> 28:06.726
Leave it and go now.
It's a 12 o'clock flight, right?

28:06.810 --> 28:08.478
It's at 11:45.

28:09.771 --> 28:12.148
I've told Mr. Park to come,
so stay close to him.

28:12.232 --> 28:14.025
I'll be back soon, okay?

28:14.109 --> 28:16.319
All right. Go on.

28:23.701 --> 28:25.745
[Iblis] I'm not sure what I wished for,

28:26.329 --> 28:29.499
but I think it led to a very grim end.

28:30.083 --> 28:31.251
So I'm scared.

28:44.639 --> 28:48.101
[soft scraping]

28:55.358 --> 28:58.319
[in Arabic] Excuse me, ma'am.
You've been rubbing this lamp

28:58.403 --> 29:00.280
for three hours now.

29:00.363 --> 29:01.990
It's only right that you buy it.

29:02.490 --> 29:04.200
It's yours for 1,000 dirhams.

29:04.784 --> 29:06.703
[in English] I cannot speak Arabic.

29:07.328 --> 29:08.872
[in Arabic] How about a discount?

29:11.833 --> 29:15.420
[Chang-Sik in Korean] Status update.
Keeping a close watch. No worries here.

29:15.503 --> 29:16.504
[Ka-young] Thank you.

29:18.882 --> 29:21.301
-[honking]
-[tires screech]

29:21.384 --> 29:22.635
[man speaking in Arabic] What?

29:22.719 --> 29:24.929
What do you want? What?

29:25.680 --> 29:27.307
[suspenseful music playing]

29:29.934 --> 29:32.687
TISAH

29:47.243 --> 29:49.037
[people gasp]

29:49.913 --> 29:51.206
[man grunts and groans]

29:59.547 --> 30:01.341
[panting]

30:02.926 --> 30:04.344
CONSULATE EMERGENCY HOTLINE

30:05.970 --> 30:06.930
[sighs]

30:18.983 --> 30:20.151
[breath trembling]

30:24.322 --> 30:26.074
Would you go easy on the rubbing?

30:30.537 --> 30:32.121
So you were avoiding me.

30:32.205 --> 30:33.790
So what if I was?

30:33.873 --> 30:36.709
When will you drop the attitude?
You'll be lucky to hit 100.

30:37.335 --> 30:41.005
You recognized me the moment you saw me.
You called me the "bitch from back then."

30:42.215 --> 30:44.133
Back when, in what time, was I that bitch?

30:45.009 --> 30:46.594
Tell me everything you know.

30:47.178 --> 30:48.513
This is my first wish.

30:48.596 --> 30:51.224
Silly girl, what the hell are you saying?

30:51.975 --> 30:54.143
I cannot grant things like wishes.

30:54.644 --> 30:57.355
Only Iblis can do that.

31:01.401 --> 31:03.111
Then I'll ask you very nicely.

31:07.198 --> 31:08.408
What's with your smile?

31:10.368 --> 31:14.330
The thing with Iblis is,
his mere presence makes us feel pathetic.

31:14.831 --> 31:17.125
He stood at the front lines in the war…

31:17.208 --> 31:18.710
[water gurgling]

31:21.212 --> 31:23.923
[Jinniya] …and he saved us
from the angels.

31:24.632 --> 31:27.176
All of us bowed our heads to you humans,

31:27.677 --> 31:30.305
but he adamantly refused
and wound up in hell.

31:30.805 --> 31:34.267
So to think the death of a mere human
made him level an entire city…

31:34.350 --> 31:36.352
I couldn't wrap my head around it.

31:37.270 --> 31:38.605
And that was me?

31:42.483 --> 31:43.484
Yes, it was you.

31:43.985 --> 31:47.572
You swept an entire city away
with gold rain. The bitch from back then.

31:49.449 --> 31:51.409
Gold rain?

31:51.492 --> 31:54.037
It was a dazzling and beautiful hell.

31:54.120 --> 31:56.080
It was the rage of Iblis.

31:56.664 --> 31:58.583
Why is his rage gold?

32:00.543 --> 32:01.794
I don't know.

32:02.378 --> 32:03.463
You don't know?

32:04.047 --> 32:05.590
I don't want to know.

32:06.799 --> 32:09.385
Why do you think Iblis has no memories?

32:12.180 --> 32:13.640
Right, I'm sorry.

32:13.723 --> 32:15.725
If you're sorry, never come back here.

32:15.808 --> 32:18.978
This cancels out the time I danced for joy
when Muttalib killed you.

32:19.062 --> 32:20.146
Go.

32:20.229 --> 32:23.107
So the jerk who killed me…

32:26.069 --> 32:26.903
Thank you.

32:30.740 --> 32:33.534
By any chance,
has Iblis ever called you habibti?

32:37.538 --> 32:39.332
Has anyone ever thrown water on you?

32:41.042 --> 32:41.876
So it was me.

32:41.960 --> 32:44.295
[thunder rumbling]

32:46.506 --> 32:47.840
[thunderclap]

32:47.924 --> 32:49.926
[pop music playing over speakers]

32:51.511 --> 32:54.514
-[sighs]
-[Sade] Irem! Irem!

32:55.682 --> 32:58.643
[panting]

33:00.687 --> 33:01.688
[sighs]

33:04.774 --> 33:07.151
Why did you ask to see me?
I just rolled out of bed.

33:08.403 --> 33:09.946
Take a seat.

33:10.029 --> 33:10.863
Sure.

33:15.326 --> 33:16.536
I don't know the details,

33:16.619 --> 33:19.122
but I have a feeling
there's more going on than we know.

33:19.205 --> 33:21.624
When that day comes,
there is something you must do.

33:23.084 --> 33:25.378
No cotton candy,
and you're already talking like that.

33:25.461 --> 33:26.629
What could be going on?

33:27.922 --> 33:30.049
You and I are both our masters' servants.

33:30.550 --> 33:34.012
So if there comes a time
when you need to make a choice,

33:34.512 --> 33:36.472
do so as your master's mythical beast.

33:37.056 --> 33:39.017
I'll decide as I should too. Got it?

33:40.643 --> 33:43.354
I came all dressed up.
What an odd way for you to dump me.

33:45.273 --> 33:47.817
Didn't you just roll out of bed?
Your ears are showing.

33:47.900 --> 33:49.027
I sleep like this.

33:49.777 --> 33:50.903
-What are those?
-How cute.

33:50.987 --> 33:53.573
-[woman] Buy me some.
-[man] Sure, let's get them.

33:57.660 --> 33:59.704
MY CHANNEL

33:59.787 --> 34:01.789
SKY FARM LIFE

34:01.873 --> 34:02.999
[exhales]

34:10.089 --> 34:13.551
NEW PASSWORD: 1 GENIE WISH IS MINE!

34:13.634 --> 34:15.386
[keyboard clacking]

34:15.470 --> 34:17.096
[suspenseful music playing]

34:17.597 --> 34:19.932
PASSWORD CHANGED

34:20.516 --> 34:21.642
[mouse clicking]

34:26.022 --> 34:27.940
YOUR CHANNEL HAS BEEN DELETED

34:30.359 --> 34:32.111
Hey, Choi Da-jin!

34:32.195 --> 34:35.364
Hey, what's wrong with our channel?
Can you access it?

34:35.948 --> 34:40.453
Damn it, the channel got deleted!
What the hell is going on?

34:42.163 --> 34:46.167
Do you think someone reported us?
This will be the death of me, damn it.

34:46.250 --> 34:47.251
No.

34:47.960 --> 34:49.337
I just deleted it.

34:49.921 --> 34:52.340
What? Are you insane?

34:52.423 --> 34:55.009
Do you know what I did
to get all those subscribers?

34:55.093 --> 34:56.385
Have you gone insane?

34:56.469 --> 34:57.512
Hey!

34:58.346 --> 35:00.807
You said to separate
what's yours and mine.

35:00.890 --> 35:03.226
I made this account under my name.

35:03.851 --> 35:07.939
If the wishes are yours,
this YouTube channel was always mine!

35:08.022 --> 35:11.234
Wow, you're completely insane!

35:11.317 --> 35:15.696
Hey, cut the bullshit.
I built it up when I found the corpse!

35:15.780 --> 35:19.033
Whatever.
Get the genie here in front of me.

35:20.159 --> 35:22.537
If we don't act in two weeks,
it's gone forever.

35:23.037 --> 35:26.582
Consider it carefully.
Only I can restore the account.

35:28.000 --> 35:31.087
Seriously, what you just did right now,

35:31.587 --> 35:33.756
you better not fucking regret it later.

35:34.715 --> 35:35.842
[breath trembling]

35:35.925 --> 35:37.677
This is my second wish.

35:37.760 --> 35:41.639
Make it so that Da-jin doesn't remember
a thing I told her about the wishes.

35:41.722 --> 35:43.224
Make her forget

35:44.559 --> 35:45.643
every single detail.

35:47.395 --> 35:48.938
Right now, damn it.

35:49.564 --> 35:51.440
[Iblis] Hey. For starters,
it's been fulfilled.

35:51.524 --> 35:54.026
I was halfway across the Gobi Desert
when you called me.

35:54.110 --> 35:56.445
This is just text,
but you can hear me, can't you?

35:56.529 --> 35:57.446
A deep, velvety voice?

35:57.530 --> 36:01.534
Did you think of a final wish
to make now too? Even if so, think more!

36:01.617 --> 36:03.369
Be grateful I'm giving you the chance,

36:03.452 --> 36:06.539
and don't use words
like "right now" or "hurry." Understand?

36:22.889 --> 36:24.223
I told you to carry the lamp.

36:24.807 --> 36:26.976
I was in a hurry,
so I left it at the hotel.

36:28.394 --> 36:31.022
I thought I might recall something,
but no luck.

36:32.023 --> 36:33.065
Man.

36:36.861 --> 36:37.862
You scared me.

36:40.990 --> 36:44.035
Hug me tighter.
It might help me recall something.

36:45.036 --> 36:46.412
What is it you want to recall?

36:46.495 --> 36:49.582
Muttalib from the sign over there.
Or the recurring villain, Khalid.

36:50.166 --> 36:53.920
Or the joy or sorrow
that you and I felt in our past lives?

36:54.003 --> 36:55.630
[chuckles]

36:55.713 --> 36:57.632
This seems strategic.

36:58.466 --> 37:00.009
You're mistaken. Hug me tighter!

37:04.180 --> 37:05.431
[Iblis grunts softly]

37:08.309 --> 37:11.062
[somber music playing]

37:20.404 --> 37:21.530
[Iblis gasps]

37:30.122 --> 37:30.957
You…

37:31.958 --> 37:34.418
You're dressed strangely today.

37:35.294 --> 37:36.712
Your hair is shorter too.

37:38.631 --> 37:39.966
Are we ready to leave?

37:40.675 --> 37:41.717
We're leaving?

37:42.593 --> 37:45.179
[chiming]

37:49.016 --> 37:50.476
You're here, so why would I?

37:52.603 --> 37:54.105
Did I have a new master?

37:56.107 --> 37:57.525
You seem a little odd today.

37:58.109 --> 37:59.527
Muttalib is your master.

38:01.028 --> 38:03.322
He must finally be ready
to make his final wish.

38:05.491 --> 38:09.912
That means we really are
leaving tonight, right?

38:11.372 --> 38:12.206
For Goryeo.

38:12.790 --> 38:14.792
Muttalib was my new master?

38:25.511 --> 38:29.056
[rumbling]

38:32.935 --> 38:33.978
[Ka-young] What's wrong?

38:40.318 --> 38:41.152
Hey.

38:42.737 --> 38:43.738
Snap out of it.

38:48.743 --> 38:50.119
There is a chance that…

38:52.079 --> 38:54.081
I never managed to get you to Goryeo.

38:57.376 --> 38:59.587
I think that's the reason my sword

39:00.588 --> 39:02.715
is stuck over there.

39:05.009 --> 39:06.010
What are you saying?

39:09.722 --> 39:10.931
Oh?

39:11.557 --> 39:12.516
You recalled something?

39:13.976 --> 39:16.479
[scoffs] It actually worked?

39:16.562 --> 39:18.356
Come here. Let's trade places.

39:23.819 --> 39:24.862
[Ka-young sighs calmly]

39:26.238 --> 39:27.156
[Iblis exhales]

39:28.115 --> 39:29.075
[exhales]

39:34.497 --> 39:38.250
[Heung-rye] I feel just the same,
so when exactly did I get so old?

39:46.842 --> 39:48.677
Oh, my, it's you!

39:48.761 --> 39:51.889
You came back without a word?
When did you get here?

39:53.391 --> 39:55.017
Hello.

39:56.727 --> 39:59.814
Good heavens,
I was so sure it was Pan-geum.

40:00.648 --> 40:01.982
I must have been mistaken.

40:02.775 --> 40:04.026
Never you mind.

40:04.819 --> 40:05.903
[Mi-ju chuckling nervously]

40:07.530 --> 40:10.658
Why the hell is she weeding a field
that isn't even hers?

40:10.741 --> 40:12.410
[Mi-ju chuckles nervously]

40:13.160 --> 40:14.745
[breathing heavily]

40:19.458 --> 40:20.501
Wait a moment.

40:27.967 --> 40:30.177
OH PAN-GEUM

40:30.261 --> 40:33.139
[automated voice] The person you've called
is currently unavailable.

40:33.222 --> 40:35.558
-Please leave a message after the beep.
-[inhales]

40:37.476 --> 40:40.646
The more I think about it,
the stranger it all gets.

40:41.147 --> 40:43.816
She sends texts
and talks with Min-ji on the phone,

40:44.316 --> 40:46.610
so why did she only cut us off?

40:47.236 --> 40:49.405
Yesterday was the anniversary
of her old man's passing.

40:50.156 --> 40:51.615
So who did the ancestral rites?

40:55.161 --> 40:57.621
[suspenseful music playing]

40:57.705 --> 40:58.539
Huh?

41:00.166 --> 41:04.086
That tramp was getting groceries
for the ancestral rites table!

41:04.837 --> 41:06.213
Goodness me.

41:06.797 --> 41:08.674
[classical music playing over speaker]

41:08.757 --> 41:11.844
[Iblis sighs] I thought you'd say
the observation deck.

41:12.511 --> 41:15.097
I don't want to stand
on the edge of anything anymore.

41:16.140 --> 41:18.309
So why did you express
your rage with gold?

41:18.392 --> 41:21.145
It was a dazzling and beautiful hell.

41:22.062 --> 41:23.731
It was the rage of Iblis.

41:23.814 --> 41:26.901
Do rage and gold even go together?

41:26.984 --> 41:28.986
Gold? What do you mean by that?

41:29.069 --> 41:31.155
Pointless if you don't remember.
Let's move on.

41:36.118 --> 41:38.704
Either way, we knew each other
during those lost 20 years.

41:39.663 --> 41:43.250
A 28-year-old you definitely existed
by my side. [clicks tongue]

41:43.918 --> 41:46.504
-But Muttalib means "foreigner."
-We just knew each other?

41:47.254 --> 41:49.632
But I was your one and only habibti.

41:49.715 --> 41:52.801
Our relationship was
definitely incredibly serious.

41:52.885 --> 41:54.887
You said it was 50-50 with Jinniya.

41:57.556 --> 41:58.766
Don't tell me…

42:01.519 --> 42:02.645
Ah.

42:02.728 --> 42:04.855
[thunder rumbling]

42:04.939 --> 42:06.190
Do you have an umbrella?

42:07.107 --> 42:08.150
[Ka-young] An umbrella?

42:09.735 --> 42:11.445
[thunderclap]

42:11.529 --> 42:13.614
Wow, this woman sure is thorough.

42:15.574 --> 42:16.575
It's raining. Kiss.

42:16.659 --> 42:18.369
[Iblis] Hey, we're in Arabia.

42:19.161 --> 42:21.205
[enthralling music playing]

42:26.377 --> 42:27.795
But it's not raining here!

42:27.878 --> 42:29.588
We broke that rule a long time ago.

42:30.548 --> 42:31.382
You didn't buy it.

42:31.465 --> 42:34.343
Man, I'm hungry.
Don't you have anything to eat?

42:35.636 --> 42:38.222
-I almost used my third wish.
-[laughs sarcastically]

42:39.056 --> 42:40.724
-Do it.
-[laughs sarcastically]

42:40.808 --> 42:42.268
Yeah, right. Give me food!

42:42.351 --> 42:45.145
[scoffs] You let me go hungry
all the time.

42:46.730 --> 42:48.107
Dry up while I set the table.

42:54.989 --> 42:56.198
Ah. Hmm.

43:02.830 --> 43:03.664
Mm.

43:15.634 --> 43:19.680
[gasps] This was here?

43:19.763 --> 43:23.392
Wait. Hey, get rid of this right now.
No, burn it quickly. Let it rot!

43:24.059 --> 43:25.436
Come on, this is…

43:25.519 --> 43:27.313
[Ka-young]
Do I look similar to my past life?

43:29.189 --> 43:30.024
What?

43:32.735 --> 43:35.696
[soft music playing]

43:48.334 --> 43:49.209
[Iblis] Yes.

43:50.836 --> 43:51.712
You look similar.

43:52.588 --> 43:53.672
Right?

43:54.465 --> 43:58.469
I also think I look
exactly as I did in the hourglass.

44:00.179 --> 44:01.930
So who's prettier? Me or her?

44:02.681 --> 44:03.891
No, don't tell me.

44:04.808 --> 44:06.226
No. Tell me.

44:06.977 --> 44:08.604
-Oh, well--
-Never mind. It's me.

44:09.605 --> 44:12.232
-[sighs]
-And what is that?

44:12.816 --> 44:14.193
-[comical music plays]
-What?

44:18.864 --> 44:19.865
What is?

44:22.326 --> 44:23.369
[gulps]

44:27.206 --> 44:28.332
Move over.

44:28.415 --> 44:29.458
It's ramyeon.

44:33.128 --> 44:37.299
Man, I told them to prepare
a proper Korean meal. [chuckles nervously]

44:41.512 --> 44:43.430
-Hmm?
-[clinking]

44:44.056 --> 44:45.099
Bring the fruit over.

44:45.182 --> 44:46.642
What? Sure.

44:48.560 --> 44:51.188
-[slurps]
-[dish clatters]

44:52.189 --> 44:53.232
[Ka-young] Mm.

44:55.776 --> 44:56.652
Mm.

44:58.362 --> 45:01.073
So do you really waltz by yourself?
Without a partner?

45:02.074 --> 45:04.118
-Waltz?
-[slurps]

45:05.285 --> 45:06.328
I've never waltzed.

45:07.621 --> 45:08.664
I don't know how.

45:09.706 --> 45:13.419
Then why do they call the sand whirls
in the desert "a waltzing genie"?

45:14.253 --> 45:15.295
Eh?

45:16.130 --> 45:16.964
[cutlery clinking]

45:17.840 --> 45:18.882
Moving on.

45:24.805 --> 45:26.056
-Fine, then.
-Hmm?

45:26.557 --> 45:28.976
Let's turn the legend into an actual fact.

45:30.853 --> 45:32.521
[slurping softly]

45:35.357 --> 45:38.485
Follow me. For old time's sake…
[cracking joints]

45:38.569 --> 45:39.820
…let's tear it up.

45:41.530 --> 45:42.573
Right.

45:45.576 --> 45:47.244
[clears throat]

45:48.912 --> 45:51.915
[soft ballad playing]

45:53.250 --> 45:56.170
[Iblis] Mm? Mm?

46:06.096 --> 46:08.849
There is a round ball
between the two of us right now.

46:08.932 --> 46:10.392
That ball is a small universe.

46:10.476 --> 46:13.645
The waltz is all about
maintaining that distance

46:13.729 --> 46:17.399
while dancing around
an even larger universe.

46:17.983 --> 46:20.152
-Do you understand?
-What? Yes.

46:20.235 --> 46:23.322
Just let yourself fall under my spell.
Follow me in a trance.

46:25.532 --> 46:26.658
Now left foot forward.

46:27.701 --> 46:30.162
[in English] One, two, three.

46:30.245 --> 46:31.288
-[in Korean] Back.
-Back.

46:31.371 --> 46:34.041
[in English] One, two, three.
[in Korean] Forward.

46:34.124 --> 46:35.584
[in English] One, two--

46:38.003 --> 46:40.214
[in Korean] Are you going
to keep stepping on my feet?

46:40.297 --> 46:42.216
This is a battle, not a dance.

46:42.799 --> 46:45.135
How is it that whatever we do,
it becomes a duel?

46:47.596 --> 46:49.973
And when exactly
did you fall under my spell?

46:50.057 --> 46:51.058
Back.

46:51.141 --> 46:53.393
[in English] One, two, three.

46:53.977 --> 46:55.646
[in Korean] The second time I saw you?

46:56.396 --> 46:57.606
But that was at the hotel.

46:58.649 --> 46:59.483
Really?

47:00.984 --> 47:02.027
That early on?

47:03.195 --> 47:05.739
Yes. I knew the moment I saw you.

47:08.075 --> 47:10.285
You come after the cars I fix.

47:10.369 --> 47:12.704
-The adjustable wrenches I grip.
-[chuckles]

47:12.788 --> 47:14.081
Let's stop. [grunts]

47:16.667 --> 47:18.377
The wheels I roll.

47:18.877 --> 47:21.713
-The hammers I use.
-I said stop. [grunts]

47:24.925 --> 47:26.593
The crowbars I use.

47:27.135 --> 47:29.263
The sound of dental scaling I like.

47:29.346 --> 47:34.560
My auto shop, gamja-tang, Grandma,

47:35.727 --> 47:37.521
Min-ji.

47:39.856 --> 47:41.191
Sea louse…

47:41.275 --> 47:43.443
[ballad continues playing]

48:08.176 --> 48:09.720
[ballad fades]

48:22.316 --> 48:24.735
[suspenseful music playing]

48:31.199 --> 48:33.076
Pan-geum definitely made this.

48:34.119 --> 48:36.955
Pan-geum, that bitch. She's here.

48:37.873 --> 48:41.126
Gosh, why is this tooth
bothering me so much?

48:41.209 --> 48:45.631
[winces] Gosh. [winces, groans]

48:46.423 --> 48:47.257
[gasps]

48:49.009 --> 48:51.261
What are you doing here, ma'am?

48:51.887 --> 48:55.807
You'd better come clean.
Where is Pan-geum?

48:56.558 --> 48:57.768
She's in Hawaii…

48:58.352 --> 48:59.603
Don't give me that crap.

49:00.270 --> 49:03.273
This tastes exactly like Pan-geum's work.
She's here, isn't she?

49:03.357 --> 49:04.399
-[hisses]
-[gasps]

49:04.483 --> 49:06.443
How dare you hide her away
while you con us!

49:07.194 --> 49:09.112
Lead the way! I need to see her now!

49:09.196 --> 49:12.074
Please let go of me.
Why are you doing this?

49:12.157 --> 49:14.326
Tramp. Where do you think
you're going? Come here.

49:16.411 --> 49:18.872
-That mole.
-[gasps]

49:18.955 --> 49:21.291
Pan-geum has that mole there too.

49:21.375 --> 49:23.293
What the hell is this?

49:23.377 --> 49:25.337
Are you Pan-geum?

49:26.004 --> 49:28.757
-Is that you, Pan-geum?
-No, I'm not!

49:30.676 --> 49:32.386
-Oh dearie!
-Dearie!

49:32.469 --> 49:36.056
Oh! You are! You are Pan-geum!

49:36.640 --> 49:39.101
[screams] It's Pan-geum!

49:40.060 --> 49:42.479
Heung-rye! Heung-rye!

49:42.562 --> 49:45.899
Good heavens! How on earth
could something like this happen?

49:45.982 --> 49:46.817
[Mi-ju] Heung-rye!

49:47.484 --> 49:50.112
Heung-rye.
Please just hear me out. Please?

49:50.195 --> 49:52.364
Let go, you wretched witch!

49:52.447 --> 49:54.658
My Lord!

49:55.158 --> 49:58.245
I was wondering where you hid her,
but you were Pan-geum all along?

49:58.745 --> 50:02.666
What the hell did you do?
How the hell did you become so young?

50:02.749 --> 50:07.879
I'll tell you everything.
So please don't tell anyone else!

50:07.963 --> 50:10.465
You disgust me. Let go, you bitch!

50:10.549 --> 50:12.342
Dear Lord!

50:12.426 --> 50:14.469
[crying] Gosh, Heung-rye. Please!

50:16.179 --> 50:18.181
[wailing]

50:19.641 --> 50:21.643
[intense music playing]

50:24.146 --> 50:26.565
[Wahid] What? That bitch is Oh Pan-geum?

50:26.648 --> 50:30.485
[chuckles] So that's how
she kept her grandma hidden.

50:31.570 --> 50:34.489
I see. That's how she used her wish.

50:34.573 --> 50:36.908
Let's start
by getting rid of that old bitch

50:36.992 --> 50:38.660
before she runs her mouth more.

50:39.369 --> 50:40.203
Ishrun.

50:40.787 --> 50:42.664
You know what to do, right?

50:47.753 --> 50:49.796
[both speaking in English]
One, two, three.

50:49.880 --> 50:51.965
Two, two, three.

50:53.633 --> 50:54.843
[in Korean] Let's go home now.

50:56.178 --> 50:57.804
I'll go and get changed.

50:58.430 --> 50:59.514
Are my clothes dry?

51:00.640 --> 51:02.350
Of course. [chuckles]

51:06.897 --> 51:09.775
[in English] One, two, three. Two, two…

51:09.858 --> 51:12.319
-[ominous music playing]
-One, two--

51:12.402 --> 51:15.405
[ominous music continues playing]

51:32.672 --> 51:36.343
-[yawns]
-[tense music playing]

52:01.827 --> 52:03.829
[soft ballad playing]
